Description: First-run onboarding tool for Linux desktops
 A first-run onboarding tool for Linux distributions: a welcome page, a
 few featured slides, and a set of interactive workflows that teach
 keyboard shortcuts by having the user actually press them.
 .
 This package is brand-agnostic: it installs no distro identity of its
 own. A distro or desktop's branding (logo, theme, slides, workflows) is
 shipped as a separate add-on package that depends on this one and drops
 its files under /usr/share/linux-onboarding/branding/<name>/, with
 /etc/linux-onboarding/branding naming which one is active. See
 /usr/share/doc/linux-onboarding/DISTRO-GUIDE.md.

